 "_source": {
  "policy": "degree-median: among nodes of the seed label with >=1 incident edge of the first-hop types, order by (degree, ID), take the element at the lower-median position (pairs.len()/2); when no node of the label carries those types, the same policy over all labels (one such template: q95, whose Comment seed label is unreachable in any LDBC output \u2014 its key records the label the policy resolved, Tag)",
  "recorded": "2026-11-01 spike, graph-benchmark-ldbc SF0.1 store (run-sf0.1.log); SF1 records from the SF1 spike subset",
  "regenerate": "seeds are store-specific \u2014 regenerate per store/scale factor with the driver (pathdb corpus lane, --seed-policy median); these values are the spike-recorded choices, kept as the pinned CI reference",
  "what": "The workload's ONE canonical seed-key fact table: one record per (seed label, first-hop types) key per scale factor (null where the key has no seed there). The key grammar is canonical \u2014 the label plus the type set sorted and de-duplicated \u2014 so one fact has exactly one spelling and the loader refuses a second; the per-SF params files carry only the derived per-query entries. Every record's label is the label of the node the policy chose and must equal its key's label \u2014 checked on load",
  "why": "0/26 original PathDB SF1 seed ids exist in our graph-benchmark-ldbc SF1 store (different datagen run); PathDB ids are not portable across LDBC datagen outputs"
